{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.705,
   "text": "I house-sat for a couple out by the lake. Their note on the fridge had one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.305,
   "end": 13.636,
   "text": "Keep the dog door latched after dark. No matter what you hear."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.636,
   "end": 21.911,
   "text": "Their old golden retriever met me at the door, tail wagging like crazy. I figured they forgot to mention him."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 22.511,
   "end": 27.524,
   "text": "Every night, he slept at the foot of my bed. The first two nights were quiet."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.324,
   "end": 34.02,
   "text": "On the third night, I woke up to scratching... and the jingle of a collar... at the dog door."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 36.62,
   "end": 41.228,
   "text": "Then whining. Soft and pitiful. Like a dog left out in the cold."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 42.428,
   "end": 47.74,
   "text": "I looked down. The golden was still at the foot of the bed. Head up. Staring at the hallway."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 48.44,
   "end": 51.085,
   "text": "He didn't bark. He didn't even blink."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 52.485,
   "end": 56.859,
   "text": "The scratching went on until sunrise. Then it just... stopped."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 58.459,
   "end": 63.365,
   "text": "In the morning, I texted the owners. Your dog was so brave last night."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 64.165,
   "end": 66.341,
   "text": "They wrote back one line."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 68.341,
   "end": 69.877,
   "text": "We don't have a dog."
  }
 ],
